SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] cycling — Shorten to 50–55 km @ 128–160W (lower
  Z2)\, approximately 180
DESCRIPTION:Shorten to 50–55 km @ 128–160W (lower Z2)\, approximately 1
 80–200 min — the day before the 5K open water race\, prioritise leg fr
 eshness over training stimulus.\n\nReason: A full 60 km ride the day befor
 e the 5K Open Water race will accumulate fatigue that undermines your swim
  performance\; a shorter\, easier spin maintains aerobic stimulus without 
 compromising race readiness.\n\nAI coaching 2026-10-10
END:VEVENT
